{"step_index":344,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:29:27Z","input_tokens":3518,"cache_read_tokens":205384,"output_tokens":1305,"thinking":"Initial validation focuses on system destination verification. The goal is to confirm the target is acceptable. This involved checking if the `entry`'s path is normalized and also if it complies with destination criteria.\n\n\nThe system destination verification checks ensure the path is within approved base files, is not protected, and doesn't overlap with overlay targets or mounts. Analysis of the `system.rs` code confirms that overlay checks are performed during the `apply` operation.  The user's problem of the release failing to install could be due to a path overlap or an issue with overlay rotation, given the error message.\n\n\nThe health check timeout causes a rollback, preventing the new release from activating. Investigation reveals the `--system` flag is rejected in the deployment script due to argument validation, specifically, it does not accept the `--system` flag. System destination validation enforces that system destinations cannot overlap overlays, explaining deployment failures due to rotating overlay targets. The relevant code is in an untracked file, meaning it isn't part of the system's normal build.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"sudo /usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release status | head -n 30","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Check current op-release status"}}]}
