{"step_index":347,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:29:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T10:29:45Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T10:29:45Z\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\nrun: op-grpc-bridge: (pid 13692) 153s; run: log: (pid 2209) 64023s\r\nrun: op-web: (pid 20205) 75s; run: log: (pid 2222) 64023s\r\nrun: emqx: (pid 15886) 127s\r\nrun: notebook-sources-sync: (pid 17643) 111s; run: log: (pid 2075) 64023s\r\n"}
{"step_index":348,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:29:46Z","input_tokens":2351,"cache_read_tokens":208886,"output_tokens":1632,"content":"The installation failure and the `--system` overlay issue stem from two specific boundaries in the release pipeline:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Why the release won't install into the slot (Rollback on Service Restore)\n\nThe Btrfs snapshot send/receive into the inactive slot (`slot b`) actually succeeds. However, during the activation phase when `op-release` rotates the read-only overlays and brings supervised services up, **`op-grpc-bridge` crashes on startup**:\n\n```text\nop-grpc-bridge: Consolidated Operation gRPC bridge starting ... plugin_id=tched_router\nError: sealed plugin not found: tched_router\n```\n\n* **Root Cause**: In recent workspace changes, `tched_router` was renamed to `chat_router` in [`crates/op-plugins`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-plugins). When `opblob seal-shm` seals the plugin catalog, it produces `chat_router.blob` instead of `tched_router.blob`. However, `op-grpc-bridge` is still configured to require `tched_router`.\n* **The Result**: `sv -w 30 check op-grpc-bridge` times out after 30 seconds. Because service restoration failed, `op-release` triggers an automatic rollback (`recovery::revert_activation`), cleanly unwinding the rotating overlays back to `slot a` and restoring the original services.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why `--system` is not working with the rotating overlay\n\nThe `--system` flag fails across three architectural gates:\n\n1. **Launcher Argument Gate ([`op-release-launch`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/deploy/release/op-release-launch#L28-L32))**:\n   `op-release-launch` enforces single-argument invocations for release commands:\n   ```sh\n   release|deploy|provision-slots|status|rollback|abort|boot) [ \"$#\" -eq 1 ] || exit 2 ;;\n   ```\n   Passing `--system` via [`deploy.sh`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/deploy.sh#L100) (`op-release-launch deploy --system`) causes the launcher to immediately exit with code 2.\n\n2. **Overlay Overlap Invariant ([`system.rs`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-deployment/src/bin/release/system.rs#L98-L99))**:\n   The base-system payload engine in `system.rs` strictly rejects any destination that overlaps with the rotating overlay mount targets:\n   ```rust\n   ensure!(targets.iter().chain(overlays).all(|p| !overlaps(&entry.path, p)),\n       \"system destination overlaps an overlay target or mount: {}\", entry.path.display());\n   ```\n   If any base payload file (e.g. under `/etc/sv/` or `/usr/local/libexec/`) overlaps an active or incoming overlay target, validation aborts before any filesystem modification.\n\n3. **Codebase Wiring Disconnect**:\n   [`crates/op-deployment/src/bin/release/system.rs`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-deployment/src/bin/release/system.rs) is currently an untracked file in the worktree and is not included (`mod system;`) in [`crates/op-deployment/src/bin/release/mod.rs`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-deployment/src/bin/release/mod.rs). Furthermore, [`build-golden.sh`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/deploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh#L742-L750) halts on unmanifested helpers left in `/opt/op-dbus/golden/libexec/3tched/` (e.g. `op-chat-responder@.service`).\n\n---\n\n### Current Host State\n\nThe host safely recovered from the failed activation:\n* **Active Slot**: `slot a` (`release-9b52e195...`) remains active and verified.\n* **Services**: `op-grpc-bridge`, `op-web`, `emqx`, `tched-router`, and `unified-execution` are all healthy and running under `slot a`.","thinking":"The release transfer places the Btrfs generation into the inactive slot. The issue surfaces during the activation phase. `op-release` is responsible for switching read-only overlays and restoring the supervised service.\n\n\nThe `op-grpc-bridge` failure stems from a plugin name mismatch; the service expects the old name, but the build process now uses the new one, causing a \"plugin not found\" error. The observed timeout and subsequent rollback are expected consequences of this startup failure, safely reverting to the previous state. The inability to use a specific deployment flag is due to an argument check in the launcher, blocking the feature. Furthermore, write operations to rotating overlays are restricted, making this integration difficult.\n\n\n"}
